Got it—here's the agent governance use case framed as a Jev API call (state = traces, questions for outcome attribution):

curl -X POST https://api.typesafe.ai/v1/systemone \
-H "Authorization: Bearer $TYPESAFE_API_KEY" \
-H "Content-Type: application/json" \
-d '{
"state": "Agent traces: [logs of actions/decisions]",
"model": "jev-latest",
"questions": {
"outcome": {"type": "choice", "instructions": "Attribute primary outcome", "criteria": {"compliant": "follows regs", "violation": "breaches policy", "ambiguous": "unclear"}},
"risk": {"type": "score", "instructions": "Score regulatory risk 0-2"},
"is_urgent": {"type": "noul", "instructions": "Needs immediate review?"}
}
}'

Fits real-time parallel assessment of millions.
